what I set out in my book fairness for  all which comes out today is that our  productivity in the UK is below the g7  average by quite a bit and what I think  is that if workers are more involved if  employees are more involved in the  success of their company then we can  improve productivity and what I talk  about is the importance of sharing  information more freely making sure that  people are empowered to shape their  future and to improve processes and  service at work but then also crucially  to make sure that some of the value  that's then created is passed back so  those that are creating the value is  that easier to do in a business like the  John Lewis Partnership than it is in a  PLC way or on support or outside  shareholders I think no if again you  look at all the evidence what it says is  that earnings per share are a hundred  and forty three percent higher in  businesses that have highly engaged  workforces so the question to ask is  what you have to do to have a highly  engaged workforce now the the chap who  set up the John Lewis Partnership  speedin Lewis was well ahead of his time  what he thought is if I look after my  people really well and they're happy and  they're engaged they're going to be more  involved in the company's success  they're going to be happier they're  going to work harder and my customers  are going to get better service and if  my customers get better service then  we're going to be more profitable and  sustainable over the long course  so what speeding lewis did about a  hundred years ago was to recognize that  there was a way of being more  sustainable and more profitable which  meant that you focused on your people  first and the shareholders ultimately  got the advantage rather than thinking  about your shareholders first and your  people last of all but if I'm a CEO how  do I do that I mean that's not something  that can be turned around overnight no  you're right I mean people have to think  very differently about th